"""Publish completed calendar/partner/track-limit evidence into local release guides."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re,html,shutil
U=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
read=lambda name:json.loads((U/'qa'/name).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
tour=json.loads((U/'src/world-tour-data.json').read_text())
design=read('circuit-design.json');limits=read('track-limits.json');partners=read('sponsor-balance.json');views=read('calendar-views.json');moving=read('moving-performance.json')
assert len(views)==12 and all(not r['errors'] and not r['audit']['assets'] for r in views)
assert len(moving['results'])==12
p=U/'docs/Validation.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s=re.sub(r'<!-- calendar-start -->.*?<!-- calendar-end -->','',s,flags=re.S)
section='''<!-- calendar-start --><h2>Full-calendar environment release</h2><p>All twelve venues passed six sampled driver views with no reported JavaScript errors or failed scene assets. The eleven real venues add terrain-fitted mapped ground areas, supporting raceways, fuller planting, boundary structures and footprint-based seating. Curved or U-shaped stands keep their open centres. Milano uses its own original ridge landscape and spectator campus. See the circuit-by-circuit environment guide for primary references and current inspection frames. These tests do not establish exact architectural fidelity or catch every possible visual defect.</p>'''
section+=f'''<p>Milano Autodromo: {design['lengthMetres']/1000:.3f} km, {design['corners']} corners, {design['elevationRangeMetres']:.0f} m elevation range, {design['minWidthMetres']:.0f}–{design['maxWidthMetres']:.0f} m widths, {design['longestStraightMetres']:.0f} m longest straight and {design['startToFirstCornerMetres']:.0f} m from the grid line to the first bend. Euler transitions, a closed periodic line and a force-constrained speed solver underpin the design. Two simulated driving laps completed without barrier contacts or invalidations. The line is a numerical local solution, not a proved global optimum or a real F1 lap prediction.</p>'''
section+='<h3>Partner allocations</h3><p>Authentic supplied logos, equal wall-wrap lengths per venue, rotated premium gantries and six equal panels on each modelled pit facade. Stand slots cycle across all six partners. Runoff artwork is restricted to paved runoff. Allocation counts do not imply equal screen time from every camera or real sponsorship of the original venues.</p><table><tr><th>Partner</th><th>Wall length, calendar</th><th>Gantry faces</th><th>Pit panels</th><th>Stand panels</th></tr>'
for name,a in partners.items():section+=f'<tr><td>{html.escape(name)}</td><td>{a["barrierMetres"]:.0f} m</td><td>{a["gantryFaces"]}</td><td>{a["pitPanels"]}</td><td>{a["standPanels"]}</td></tr>'
section+='</table><h3>Forgiving track limits</h3>'
section+=f'''<p>The default event rule permits kerb/tyre overlap and brief recovery beyond the edge. The car-centre allowance is 2.4 m outside the road edge; shallow excursions get up to one second or 70 m. Deeper shortcuts use a shorter 0.25-second or 18 m threshold. A continuous excursion generates one event and rearms after 0.45 seconds safely inside the recovery corridor. Qualifying and timed practice delete sustained-cut laps; races warn three times before adding five seconds on the fourth event. Online races use the same policy. Surface grip fades gradually beyond the kerb, independently of penalties.</p><p>{limits['scenarioChecks']:,} scenario checks cover both sides and the narrowest/widest sections of every circuit at three update rates. {limits['serverBrowserParityTraces']} traces produced identical browser and Python event indices. The server integration also tests kerb use and four separate excursions on every venue. These are deliberately accessible game rules, not the FIA track-limit procedure.</p>'''
section+='<h3>Moving-grid render sample</h3><p>1440×900 Ultra on the RTX 3050 laptop. Twenty-one AI drivers accelerate from the grid while the player remains stationary; the last eight seconds are sampled after a two-second warm-up. This exercises moving AI and rendering together, but does not represent a complete race or minimum FPS throughout a lap. During the longer run, a hardware sample showed 89°C GPU temperature and 100% utilization; frame intervals were more variable than the short isolated foliage checks. Results below retain that variation rather than promising a locked frame rate.</p><table><tr><th>Venue</th><th>Median frame</th><th>95th percentile</th></tr>'
for r in moving['results']:section+=f'<tr><td>{html.escape(tour[r["id"]]["name"])}</td><td>{r["medianMs"]:.1f} ms</td><td>{r["p95Ms"]:.1f} ms</td></tr>'
section+='</table><p>The home showroom is capped at 30 fps and opaque settings at 4 fps while input and network polling continue. Driving is uncapped. Distant overlapping foliage uses stable world-cell canopy selection; nearby full geometry remains. Distant canopy impostors no longer sample the near-car shadow map. This removes redundant distant shading while retaining the wooded setting.</p><!-- calendar-end -->'
s=s.replace('<h2>Geometry and sporting scope</h2>',section+'<h2>Geometry and sporting scope</h2>')
s=s.replace('5.033 km, 15-corner','6.540 km, 17-corner').replace('six-second frame-interval samples','eight-second frame-interval samples').replace('six seconds after warm-up','eight seconds after warm-up')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=U/'docs/Circuit Research.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('Original 5.033 km, 15-turn circuit','Original 6.540 km, 17-turn circuit').replace('48 m of designed elevation','74 m of designed elevation').replace('constant 16 m','14–18 m');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=U/'docs/Race Weekend Guide.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s=re.sub(r'<!-- event-limits -->.*?<!-- /event-limits -->','',s,flags=re.S);s=s.replace('</main>','<!-- event-limits --><h2>Use the kerbs</h2><p>Brief run-offs have a recovery window. Sustained or deep cuts delete timed laps. In races, the first three excursions earn warnings; the fourth adds five seconds. One trip off track counts once. Online and solo races use the same forgiving policy. Reset penalties and checkpoint checks still apply.</p><!-- /event-limits --></main>');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
shutil.copy2(U/'qa/milano-design.png',U/'docs/inspection/milano-design.png')
p=U/'PROGRESS.txt';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');marker='\nCalendar release 23 October 2026:';s=s.split(marker)[0]+marker+' All twelve circuits received an environment and partner-placement pass. Milano is a 6.540 km, 17-corner ridge circuit with 74 m elevation range. Real venues gain mapped terrain-fitted surfaces, denser planting, supporting routes and footprint-based stands. All six partners have rotated gantries and equal modelled pit facade allocations. Forgiving track limits permit kerb use and brief excursions; races warn before penalties and the Python host shares the same rule. Distant canopy LOD reduces forest overdraw. Local visual, numerical, multiplayer, UI, offline and GPU evidence is in the release guides. Reconstruction and hardware limits remain explicit. No public game deployment performed.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
print('Updated calendar, partner and track-limit release evidence.')
